## Facts (from doc/plan/c016-worklog/core-send-routing-id-assert-summary.md, unresolved item 2)
REJECT closes the duplicate pipe with `terminate(true)` (`router_admission.cpp` ~366/461). On the connector side a ROUTER socket has the
peer's routing-id preamble staged in the pipe; termination leaves the pipe in `waiting_for_delimiter` until an application recv drains the
preamble, so the monitor DISCONNECTED edge (and the reconnect per connect intent) is delayed until the application happens to recv. A DEALER
connector observes DISCONNECTED immediately. Reproduce with the public API: ROUTER(RID A) connects to ROUTER(REJECT policy) twice (or a second
socket with the same RID) so the second pipe is rejected; the connector never calls recv; assert DISCONNECTED for the rejected connection_id
arrives within the command-progress bound with only `zlink_socket_monitor_recv`/`zlink_poll` on the monitor (no app recv) — this fails today.

